<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lealui</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lealui is the dry-season capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/litunga">Litunga</a>, the king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lozi-people">Lozi</a>, on the Barotse floodplain of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a>, near Mongu. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lewanika">Lewanika</a> made it his capital in the late nineteenth century. Each year, as the flood rises, the Litunga leaves Lealui for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limulunga">Limulunga</a> on higher ground in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomboka">Kuomboka</a> ceremony, returning when the waters fall.</p></div>
